# M / B017 — security-scan/references/scan-layers.md, security-scan.

C R202 OL WF-020 | MUST | Security review requires evidence and contextual severity: investigation prompts are not automatic vulnerability declarations; report concrete risks, distinguish confirmed findings from items needing verification, rate severity by exploitability, reachability, exposure and impact rather than mechanically by pattern, CVSS or OWASP category; avoid known false positives; do not claim a static scan proves design security; do not invent exploitability; do not upgrade packages during a scan unless asked. | security review | none stated
C R203 OL WF-021 | MUST NOT | The security scan must work without any specific MCP server, agent, analyzer, commercial scanner or other external tool; available tooling is evidence, never the sole authority, and a scanner-reported issue is reported only after inspecting the actual code and its reachability. | security review | none stated
C X23 EX WF-020 | MUST | Security findings are reported in a fixed shape: severity tag, file:line location and title, OWASP category when applicable, Evidence, Impact (why it is a risk) and Remediation; uncertain findings use the NEEDS VERIFICATION form stating what effective behavior depends on. | security review output | none stated | WF-020 requires evidence and contextual severity; the oracle does not prescribe a security finding format. | A finding without Evidence/Impact/Remediation sections does not follow the workflow.
C X24 EX WF-020,WF-009 | MUST | The security scan report contains Scope, a Limitations statement (static analysis only), a severity Summary table, Findings and Layer Results for the seven layers using PASS / FINDINGS / NOT APPLICABLE / NOT CHECKED, with the fixed severity scale Critical / High / Medium / Low / Info and defined meanings. | security scan output | none stated | WF-020/WF-009 require contextual severity and truthful status reporting; the oracle does not prescribe report sections, layer tables or a severity scale. | A scan report without the limitations statement or layer results table does not follow the workflow.

